s7-6-p11 : Block
s7-6-p11 = prose (cons "Let `o-idh c = o-issue c`, and `o-comph h₁ h₂ c = o-handle h₂ (h₁ c)`. Induction constructs paths witnessing the identity and composition laws for handlers. In particular, the inductive proof of `o-handle-id` has the return case by reflexivity and the command case by congruence over the recursively handled continuation; `o-handle-bind` is proved by induction, using associativity of `o-bind` at command nodes. Thus handler composition is a computed property of these programs, not a special semantics imposed by the host language." nil)
